WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right!
What's going on, everybody?

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
Good to see you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:06.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know
what you all are thinking --

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.007 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"DJ Khaled!"

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
No, I'm just kidding.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Another one!"
You guys are very...

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:14.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
accurately racist, actually.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
My name is Mohammed --
it's not Khaled.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.184 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I live in New York now.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:21.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've had
like 20 Mohammed Uber drivers

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:24.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the last week alone.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:25.358 line:92%
Every time I get a notification

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:26.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
that a Mohammed
is going to pick me up,

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:27.627 line:92%
I always make a stupid face.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:30.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Hey, all right.
My man, all right!"

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:31.064 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then,
I start imagining that,

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.867
when he gets the notification
that he's picking up Mohammed,

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:37.604
he's making the same stupid face
as I am at the same exact time.

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:39.172
"He's like, all right, Mohammed!
Salaam alaikum, brother!

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm coming to get you!"
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.878 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:47.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am
a Palestinian-American Muslim,

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:48.882 size:84% position:42% line:92%
came here as a refugee.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:52.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yay! Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:53.820 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Chuckles ]

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.822
It's a tough time to be Mohammed
right now.

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:56.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
Uh.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
I traveled the world
without a passport for --

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
It took me 20 years
to get my citizenship.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would get interrogated
everywhere.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:04.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
Japan, by far,
my favorite interrogation --

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:07.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was just an hour
of them trying to figure out

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
what I did for a living.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:13.673
The entire hour consisted of,
"So, what is your occupation?"

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:16.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"Oh, I'm a comedian."

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.911 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Comedian?"

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:18.812 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:20.547 line:92%
"Yeah, I do stand-up comedy."

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:22.582 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Stand-up comedy?"

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:23.550 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.918 line:92%
"Yeah, man, I do comedy."

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:25.518 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Comedy?"

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:26.886 line:92%
"Yeah, I'm a stand-up comedian."

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Stand-up comedian?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Am I being roasted right now?
What's happening?"

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.392 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.160 line:92%
Finally, his friend walks in.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
His friend walks in.
He's like, "...comedian."

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.933 line:92%
He goes, "Oh, yeah, comedian.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:42.168 size:88% position:44% line:92%
He's like a Bill Cosby!"

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.103 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:46.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's what got me off
was Bill Cosby.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:46.573 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, not literally,
but figuratively --

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's what...
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:53.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
What? What'd I say? What?
[ Applause ]

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:56.716 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.318 line:92%
London was always exciting.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:59.686 line:92%
I get there, and they're like,

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:00.887 size:78% position:39% line:92%
[British accent] "Oh!

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:03.656 line:92%
Oh, hello, Mohammed, hello.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:06.292 size:88% position:44%
We need your thumbprint.
Yeah, your thumbprint."

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:09.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Eventually, I get through.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:10.230 line:92%
I was performing in London.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
This guy in the front row --
I look at him.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:12.866 line:92%
I was like, "Excuse me sir.

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
What part of England
are you from?"

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:15.435 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He loses his mind.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:20.273
He was like, "I'm not British --
I'm Australian!

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:21.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
Aussie, Aussie, Aussie!"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
And all these Australians
popped up like little minions,

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, "Oi, oi, oi, oi,
oi, oi, oi!"

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:27.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I was like, "Oh, hey.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hold up. Hold up.
Hold up, please."

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:30.316 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:34.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't realize
it was so offensive...

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
to mistake an Australian
for being British.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I just looked at him.

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:39.192 line:92%
I was like, "My God, man,

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
the British flag
is inside of your flag!"

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:42.996 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:45.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
"It's in
the top-left-hand corner,

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:47.200 size:81% position:41% line:92%
FaceTiming your flag."

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.203 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:55.375 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.410 size:81% position:41% line:92%
[ Applause continues ]

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
They asked me to do shows
for U.S. troops.

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:02.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought
it was a setup immediately.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I was -- was like,

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:04.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Who is this?!"
[ Chuckles ]

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:07.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're like, "No, we want you
to go to Kuwait and Iraq."

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:09.489 size:84% position:42%
I'm like, "That's where
my family fled from!"

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:10.023 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:12.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You want me to go back
into a war zone voluntarily --

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll do it."
Yeah.

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:15.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't know
where you're going.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:16.763 line:92%
And we were in Northern Iraq.

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're about to walk off
the base --

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:19.232 line:92%
me and the two other comedians.

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:21.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the sergeant looks at us
and goes, "Hey, fellas,

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
uh, make sure
to remove your nametags,

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:26.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
cause I don't want you guys
getting kidnapped."

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:30.376 size:84% position:42%
I was like, "Kidnapped?
We can get kidnapped?"

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:31.144 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I started to freak out.

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:33.880 size:81% position:41%
And then I remembered
I'm in Kuwait and Iraq

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.816
and I look like
everybody else there, you know?

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:37.517 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:38.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
If anybody's
gonna get kidnapped,

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:40.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's probably these
two very white comedians

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:42.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm working with.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some terrorists
were to hop out of a van like,

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:48.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey! Hey, it's a kidnapping!
Get in the van now!"

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:50.563 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I'd be like, "Habibi..."

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:53.333 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:56.369 line:92%
[ Speaking foreign language ]

00:03:56.369 --> 00:04:00.506 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.842 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:05.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm sorry, guys."
[ Chuckles ]

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:08.181 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:10.650 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you very much.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:11.784 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank you.

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:14.120 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:14.954 line:92%
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:19.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much for coming.
-[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:19.926 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:24.330
-Mo Amer! Mo Amer!
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:29.335
Check out his comedy special
"The Vagabond" on Netflix.

